    cursor: pointer;
    transition: border-color var(--vds-file-upload-transition-duration)
      var(--vds-file-upload-transition-easing),
      box-shadow 180ms ease-out;

    /* ── Radius nesting host ──
       The "Browse" chip is welded to this control's inner edge, so it has to
       carry the control's corner minus the 1px border. That used to be done by
       `overflow: hidden`, which works but clips anything a consumer puts
       inside, focus rings included; there is no scrollport here, so real
       corner inheritance is the better tool. All three are declared, zeroes
